␀ห?”๐␀␀␀␀␀หฟÜ␀␀␀␀␀ห?h␀␀␀␀␀ห?␀␀␀␀␀หฟ␀␀␀␀␀ห?@␀␀␀␀␀หฟ•ิ␀␀␀␀␀ข42ขidู0cli-enhancements-discussion-cli-enhancements-006งcontentฺ## Should tags and type be settable at creation only, or also via update?

### Context
Need to decide lifecycle of new fields โ€” create-only or mutable via update? And if mutable, how to handle clearing.

### Journey
Straightforward that both create and update should support all three fields (tags, type, refs). The interesting question was clearing. The `--clear-description` pattern already exists โ€” it was added specifically because empty `--description ""` was erroring, and agents were accidentally erasing descriptions. Same protective philosophy applies here: empty values on `--tags`/`--refs`/`--type` should error, clearing requires an explicit flag.

### Decision

**All fields settable on both create and update. Replace semantics.**

- `--tags`, `--refs`, `--type` on create: set initial values
- `--tags`, `--refs`, `--type` on update: replace entire value
- Empty value on any of them: error (protective against accidental erasure)
- `--clear-tags`, `--clear-refs`, `--clear-type`: explicit clearing flags
- Mutually exclusive: `--tags` and `--clear-tags` can't be used together (same as `--description` / `--clear-description`)

