### Context
Tasks have two relationship types: parent/child (decomposition) and dependencies (ordering). Should the dep tree mix them?

### Decision
**Dependencies only. No parent/child relationships, no parent annotations.**

Parent/child and dependencies have different semantics โ€” decomposition vs ordering. Mixing them in one tree creates ambiguity (is B under A because A blocks B, or because B is a child of A?). Considered annotating parent info inline (e.g., `(child of tick-a1b2)`) but parent hierarchies can be multiple levels deep, making annotations messy and noisy.

The command is `tick dependency tree` โ€” it shows dependencies. Parent/child hierarchy visualization is a separate feature if ever needed.

