### Key Insights
1. Only dependency blockers propagate down the ancestor chain โ€” "has open children" is structural, not a sequencing constraint
2. Full ancestor chain traversal needed to avoid gaps with intermediate grouping tasks
3. Recursive CTE is the right tool โ€” established pattern in codebase, shallow chains make performance a non-issue

### Current State
- All questions resolved
- Clear implementation path identified

### Next Steps
- [ ] Implement `ReadyNoBlockedAncestor()` helper
