␀␀␀␀␀หฟ␀␀␀␀␀ห?T␀␀␀␀␀ห?–$␀␀␀␀␀หฟ‘่␀␀␀␀␀ห?D␀␀␀␀␀ห?‘L␀␀␀␀␀ฃ223ขidู+v1-specification-blocked-ancestor-ready-001งcontentฺ ## Problem

Children of blocked parents incorrectly appear as "ready" in `tick ready` and `tick list --ready`. The current ready check uses 3 conditions (open status, no own unclosed blockers, no open children) but never checks whether the task's parent โ€” or any ancestor โ€” is itself dependency-blocked.

### Example

```
Phase 1 (open)
Phase 2 (open, blocked_by: Phase 1)
  โ””โ”€ subtask-A (open)    โ shows as "ready" despite Phase 2 being blocked
  โ””โ”€ subtask-B (open)    โ same
```

The subtasks pass all ready checks because they personally have no blockers โ€” only their parent does.

### Current Implementation

`internal/cli/query_helpers.go` defines:
- `ReadyConditions()` โ€” 3 conditions: open status, no unclosed blockers, no open children
- `BlockedConditions()` โ€” De Morgan inverse: open status AND (has unclosed blocker OR has open children)
- Both use simple EXISTS/NOT EXISTS subqueries against `dependencies` and `tasks` tables
- No ancestor traversal anywhere

### Affected Code Paths

| File | Usage |
|------|-------|
| `internal/cli/query_helpers.go` | `ReadyConditions()`, `BlockedConditions()`, `ReadyWhereClause()` |
