␀␀หฟsü␀␀␀␀␀ห?␀␀␀␀␀ห?t␀␀␀␀␀ห?ฐ€␀␀␀␀␀หฟฤ␀␀␀␀␀ห?ไ␀␀␀␀␀ห?V8␀␀␀␀␀ห?␀␀␀␀␀ห?␀␀␀␀␀ห?s␀␀␀␀␀ฃ273ขidูGready-includes-in-progress-specification-ready-includes-in-progress-006งcontentฺ	 ## Affected Code Surface

These are implementation shapes captured from the discussion โ€” concrete enough to plan against, not prescriptive line-by-line.

### `internal/cli/query_helpers.go` โ€” the status gate

The shared `t.status = 'open'` literal in **both** `ReadyConditions()` and `BlockedConditions()` becomes `t.status IN ('open','in_progress')`. The `negateNotExists` / inverse machinery that derives `BlockedConditions()` from the ready conditions is **untouched** โ€” the symmetry is exactly why this is a one-line-per-side change. `ReadyWhereClause()` (consumed by `stats`) picks up the new gate automatically.

### `internal/cli/list.go` โ€” conditional `ORDER BY` in `buildListQuery`

The `ORDER BY` becomes conditional on the ready filter. When `f.Ready`, prepend a status-priority term โ€” e.g. `ORDER BY (t.status = 'in_progress') DESC, t.priority ASC, t.created ASC`; otherwise the current `t.priority ASC, t.created ASC` clause is unchanged. Keyed on `f.Ready`, so it applies to both `tick ready` and `tick list --ready` and to neither `tick list` nor `tick list --blocked`.

When the result set contains zero `in_progress` rows, the `(t.status = 'in_progress') DESC` term is uniformly false and a no-op, so the ordering is byte-identical to the current `priority ASC, created ASC`. This is the basis for the no-regression criteria (AC #2, #6) โ€” a ready list with no in-flight work is unchanged.

### `internal/cli/stats.go` โ€” blocked derivation + comment

Change the blocked count from `Open โ’ Ready` to `(Open + InProgress) โ’ Ready`. Two comments need refreshing (reference by content, not line number โ€” numbers drift): the **ready-count** comment (`// Ready count: open, no unclosed blockers, no open children.`) โ’ `// Ready count: open or in_progress, no unclosed blockers, no open/in-progress children, no blocked ancestor.`; and the **blocked-count** comment (`// Blocked count: open AND NOT ready (derived from ready).`) โ’ `// Blocked count: live (open or in_progress) AND NOT ready, derived as (Open + InProgress) โ’ Ready.`

### No changes required

- State machine โ€” confirmed: `start` constrains only `from: open`, no blocker guard; blockers stay a query-time concept. No transition logic changes.
- Flag registry / `commandFlags` โ€” no new flags added; `--status` and `--count` already valid on `ready`.
- Formatters โ€” no presentation change in any format.
