When a child task transitions to `in_progress`, its parent (and ancestors) remain `open` until manually started. This feels wrong โ€” if you're working on a subtask, the parent is implicitly in progress. The question is whether Tick should automatically cascade status changes upward through the ancestor chain, and what the implications are.

The primary pain point: parent containers sit as "open" and never get closed out, especially when AI agents (Claude) are working through subtasks via the workflow system. Parents get neglected.

